ught years ago there  was always somebody out there  that can clean your clock eventually  and so i worked on my fundamentals and  worked on play i just loved the  competition i didn't feel anything that  i was any better than anybody else i  used to watch players and see what  they'd do see demons to me is action  reaction with the subtleties right well  you got i know you're playing against i  mean like jerry west was the logo if he  got the shoot he's going to make it you  know bart frazier was tough on defense  russell liked the black shots you were  an advocate for protecting players  financially but also you stood for  social equality you played in a time  where let's just be honest  it wasn't easy to be a black man in  america well no but you know but i think  sports i once said that  the greatest event for me was the  olympics i'm on a stand with jerry west  i said man how the hell would get here  i said i was born in tennessee i said  man this is the greatest thing i've ever  experienced in my life you're up there  you hear the natural anthem man that  goes all through you  it was something i would never ever  forget ray allen from the university of  connecticut it is october 15 1996. so i  get drafted earlier that year in june  1996 and it said first game minnesota  timberwolves second chicago bulls united  center october 15  1996.  and you know i've never met michael  jordan before in my life right and so i  was you know i was scared to death  thinking what was i going to be able to  give to the game because you're a fan of  jewelry yeah still posters on this wall  on my wall like wearing shoes like all  this and i'm like i'm about to play  against the greatest that i've ever seen  and so  that that day comes we're in the united  stand i just remember sitting on the  court i was stretching and then the  whole song comes out and i was like man  i'm really into tv right now  yeah i've been hearing this this opening  montage of the bulls stampeding through  